{{also|Dinar|dînar}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Derived from Roman currency name [[denarius]].

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# Name of official [[currency]] of several countries, including [[Algeria]], [[Bahrain]], [[Iran]], [[Iraq]], [[Jordan]], [[Kuwait]], [[Libya]], [[Serbia]], [[Sudan]], [[Yemen]] and [[Tunisia]].
# A coin or note worth one dinar.

